THIRD-PARTY SOFTWARE
--------------------

HERO takes no NuGet dependencies. It is built entirely against the .NET base
class libraries, WPF, and in-box Windows APIs. There is no vendored third-party
source in this repository.

The self-contained build is the one exception, and it is a packaging one rather
than a source one: `dotnet publish --self-contained` embeds the .NET runtime and
the WPF assemblies into the single HERO.exe it produces. Those are Microsoft's
work, licensed under the MIT License, and the MIT License requires its notice to
travel with substantial portions of the software.

The .NET SDK does not copy those notices into publish output, so they are shipped
alongside the binary deliberately. They are reproduced in
THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt, taken verbatim from the runtime pack that produced the
build (microsoft.netcore.app.runtime.win-x64).

Microsoft.Windows.SDK.NET.dll, present in the framework-dependent build, ships
under the Windows SDK licence terms rather than MIT. Those terms permit
redistribution inside an application and impose no notice condition, so nothing
is required here for it. See https://aka.ms/WinSDKLicenseURL.
